<title>PORTUGAL: INSTANT VIEW - BTA 1996 results.</title>
<headline>INSTANT VIEW - BTA 1996 results.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are reactions to the 1996 results of Portuguese bank Banco Totta e Acores which reported a profit of 15.6 billion escudos, down from 17.2 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>JOSE FREIRE, ESPIRITO SANTO RESEARCH:</p>
<p>&quot;I think share prices of the banks of businessman Antonio Champalimaud will not show strong reactions because the results were in line with expectations. There is some suspense over the dividends.&quot;</p>
<p>JOAO VERMELHO, CENTRAL DE INVESTIMENTOS</p>
<p>&quot;BTA's profit was slightly above expectations, but the share price will not be significantly affected.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Paula Cordeiro, Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
